<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">păvesco</span></b> , ĕre,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
			n.</i> and <i>a.</i> [paveo] (mostly post-Aug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to begin to be
			afraid</i>, <i>to become alarmed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omni strepitu pavescere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 72, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad ejusmodi tactum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 6,
					2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad nocturnas imagines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					29, 4, 20, § 67</span></i>
			 (al. expavescere): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pavescere sensim et quasi albescere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 19, 1, 21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to begin to fear</i> or
				<i>dread</i>, <i>to begin to be
				alarmed at</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prodigia deūm,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					16, 127</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
